id: pm-web-pep7
title: Surface optional package requirements for maintenance command routes
description: "Reproduction with the pinned CLI and a fresh real PM workspace: GET pm/comments-audit and POST pm/normalize return HTTP 200 with an unknown_command error requiring pm-governance-audit; POST pm/reindex with mode keyword returns HTTP 400 requiring pm-search-advanced. The default package provides these UI actions without provisioning or capability guidance for their newly optional providers. Covered through real HTTP/PostgreSQL in test/pm-command-access.test.ts. Follow-up: expose provider availability and actionable install guidance, preserve all authorization and refusal paths, and use appropriate non-success status for a refused operation. Optional package provisioning and UI capability migration are outside the route coverage task pm-web-ulgy."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-16T03:55:57.787Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:36:06.371Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:36:05.000Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:36:05.000Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Fresh workspaces expose which maintenance actions require optional providers; Unavailable actions return an actionable documented non-success response without modifying tracker state; Real HTTP and PostgreSQL tests cover provider availability and preserve authorization and CSRF refusals
resolution: "Reverified main ca7e188bc91e (unchanged since audit): [PR #213](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/213) (02bb294) returns typed provider-unavailable responses and #215 (54c694b) keeps Packages usable when capability reads fail. Retained evidence: public/src/sw.ts, public/src/views/comments-audit.ts, public/src/views/maintenance.ts."
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T10:42:51.841Z",codex-agent,"Preserved the existing issue and append-only history from the route-coverage branch because they are not yet on main. Verified the pinned SDK packageInstall flow accepts pm-governance-audit and pm-search-advanced as bundled aliases, activating builtin-governance-audit and builtin-search-advanced. Design: bounded per-project SDK command-describe cache, invalidated by package mutations; HTTP 424 provider_unavailable with package and role-aware Packages guidance; extensions endpoint maintenance capabilities; guarded UI views; bundled catalog entries without automatic provisioning. Preserve view-only mutation 403 and foreign-project 404."
  "2026-10-16T10:49:14.711Z",codex-agent,"Focused linked acceptance passed 33/33 with zero failures, skips or cancellations: env PM_FLEET_ROOT=../../fleet node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test test/maintenance-providers.test.ts test/maintenance-ui.test.ts test/catalog.test.ts test/extensions-routes.test.ts. Real HTTP/PostgreSQL verifies owner/editor hints, viewer read hints without install, viewer mutation 403, foreign 404, CSRF refusal, both actual bundled installs and command outputs, project isolation, disable/enable/uninstall, failed-read recovery and external-install cache expiry. Bundled catalog command metadata is checked against real SDK installation receipts. The canonical fleet root avoids the existing partial-sibling discovery issue pm-web-4p94. Replaced the not-yet-merged command-access file link with the regression files in this branch."
  "2026-10-16T10:49:15.733Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs: with only the maintenance route callbacks restored from main, node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"missing providers return typed\" test/maintenance-providers.test.ts failed 200 versus expected 424 after rebuilding server output. Restoring only the extensions GET callback failed its role/capability assertion (undefined versus true). Removing only invalidateMaintenanceCapabilities cache eviction failed the real bundled install test (false versus true). Restoring only renderNormalizeView from main, rebuilding frontend output, and running node --test --test-name-pattern=\"maintenance views check capabilities\" test/maintenance-ui.test.ts failed because the disabled requirement was absent and an unavailable command was attempted. All source restored and server/frontend rebuilt after proofs; each selected regression exited 1 under its revert."
  "2026-10-16T11:00:39.306Z",codex-agent,"Additional validation: both source and built server catalog-install acceptance, canonical fleet command metadata, and maintenance provider lifecycle passed 23/23 with no failures/skips/cancellations. The first full npm run was 621/624: two catalog roster assertions needed the new bundled entries; the optional live command freshness check needed a resolved fleet root for its dependency symlinks. Corrected the roster and use PM_FLEET_ROOT=\"$(realpath ../../fleet)\" for full gates. SDK package describe includes global claims even with project scope; project capabilities now project that public activation-ordered ownership table onto project claims, matching isolated maintenance execution. A real bundled provider installed only in a disposable global home is not advertised. Reverting only that projection failed the global-only regression (true versus false); restored afterward."
  "2026-10-16T11:26:40.492Z",codex-agent,"Final gates passed on unchanged source: env HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 PM_FLEET_ROOT=\"$(realpath ../../fleet)\" npm run release:check; the identical environment with bun run release:check also passed. Each full suite: 625/625, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos; capacity acceptance 1/1 with 20 authenticated subscribers and five mixed writer lanes; four packed-consumer scenarios (npm/Bun, minimum/current host) accepted; production audit zero vulnerabilities; typecheck/lint/docstrings/zero duplication/changelog/date/publish-attestation checks passed. Coverage: npm statements/lines 91.13%, branches 81.39%, functions 94.29%; Bun statements/lines 91.13%, branches 81.41%, functions 94.29%. No capacity timing flake observed. Existing fleet-root limitations are tracked in pm-web-4p94. The linked regression command now uses only task-specific HTTP/UI/extension tests and works without a sibling fleet; its final receipt is current. No hosted changes."
  "2026-10-16T11:27:16.457Z",codex-agent,"Portable final linked regression run passed 16/16 through pm test pm-web-pep7 --run --progress (exit 0, reported_tests receipt; zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos). Implementation and package-owned evidence are ready for PR review; claim released while the issue remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-16T11:29:46.959Z",codex-agent,"Current main merged the original route-coverage task while this branch ran its gates, causing an add/add conflict on the same issue. The incoming history was verified byte-for-byte as an exact prefix of this branch history; preserved the complete existing superset without re-anchoring, repairing or rewriting any record. The PM merge driver refused the add/add despite that shared prefix; report this upstream behavior without filing or patching it here. Updated the newly merged command-access regression to require HTTP 424, provider_unavailable, the actual provider and Packages guidance. Retained the newly ratcheted main coverage thresholds unchanged. Reclaimed for merge integration and fresh gates."
  "2026-10-16T11:44:48.455Z",codex-agent,"Merged-main validation: npm run release:check passed 644/644 tests, capacity 1/1 and four packed consumers, with unchanged main thresholds (92.07 statements/lines, 80.5 branches, 94.59 functions). Measured coverage 92.46 statements/lines, 81.15 branches, 95.98 functions. Additional behavioural revert: restoring only the old maintenance route callbacks and running node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"maintenance and static command\" test/pm-command-access.test.ts failed 200 versus expected 424 (exit 1). Restored the exact source bytes and rebuilt server output afterward. The updated original reproduction now independently detects the old silent-success behavior."
  "2026-10-16T11:58:41.628Z",codex-agent,"Final merged-tree evidence: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed with isolated Git identity and resolved canonical fleet root. Each completed 644/644 tests (zero fail/skip/cancel/todo), capacity acceptance 1/1 and all four npm/Bun minimum/current packed consumers. Both measured 92.46% statements/lines, 81.15% branches, 95.98% functions, clearing current main thresholds unchanged (92.07/92.07/80.5/94.59). Audit zero vulnerabilities; typecheck/lint/zero duplication/docstrings/changelog/date/publish-attestation all passed. No capacity timing flake observed. The portable linked command now includes the original command-access regression and passed 25/25 through pm test --run --progress. No runtime source changes followed these gates. Claim released for orchestrator verification; issue remains in progress."
  "2026-10-16T15:28:19.439Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: address the capability-read failure independently from package discovery. Preserve package rows and owner install controls, return a typed unavailable capability state, log the failure, and verify owner/viewer behavior through real HTTP/PostgreSQL tests plus a behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-10-16T15:31:32.934Z",codex-agent,"Implemented independent capability-read handling: HTTP 200 retains real package inventory and caller edit permission; unavailable reads omit maintenance availability, return capabilities_unavailable with a safe message, and log redacted diagnostics. Packages retain owner/editor controls with a non-blocking warning. Maintenance views fail closed. The application exposes a narrow capability-reader wiring seam while inventory, SDK, authentication and PostgreSQL remain real in acceptance tests."
  "2026-10-16T15:32:58.705Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: restored only the extensions GET capability-read behavior to an unguarded await while retaining the injected real application seam and regression. node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"capability-read failures\" test/maintenance-providers.test.ts exited 1: 0/1 passed, HTTP 500 versus required 200. Restored the exact source bytes and rebuilt server output. With the fix present the same focused test passed 1/1. Acceptance uses real PostgreSQL, auth, package inventory and a real installed bundled provider; no SDK mock. Lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass."
  "2026-10-16T15:34:50.402Z",codex-agent,"The portable linked HTTP/UI/extension/command-access regression passed through pm test pm-web-pep7 --run --progress: 26/26 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. The new capability-read regression renders the actual HTTP responses for owner and viewer, verifies installed and uninstalled package rows and owner controls, refuses every maintenance action, and confirms redacted failure logging. Starting both release gates with isolated Git identity and the existing canonical fleet catalog input."
  "2026-10-16T15:56:43.194Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check passed with isolated Git identity and canonical fleet catalog input: 645/645 tests, capacity acceptance 1/1, all four packed consumers, zero production vulnerabilities, and all typecheck/lint/duplication/docstring/changelog/date/publish-attestation checks. Zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos; no timing flake observed. Coverage: 92.48% statements/lines, 81.18% branches, 96.00% functions, above the unchanged 92.07/92.07/80.5/94.59 thresholds. Starting bun run release:check against unchanged runtime source."
  "2026-10-16T16:17:34.950Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 final local gates: bun run release:check also passed completely with isolated Git identity and canonical fleet input: 645/645 tests, capacity 1/1, all four npm/Bun minimum/current packed consumers, zero production vulnerabilities, and every remaining release check. Coverage was 92.54% statements/lines, 81.30% branches, 96.00% functions. npm measured 92.48/92.48/81.18/96.00. Both retain unchanged thresholds 92.07/92.07/80.5/94.59; neither had failures, skips, cancellations, todos or timing flakes. Linked acceptance passed 26/26; the behavioral revert failed HTTP 500 versus 200 and was restored exactly. No runtime source changes followed these gates. Releasing the claim while the item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; pushing the implementation and evidence for GitHub checks."
  "2026-10-16T16:20:31.848Z",codex-agent,"Delivery update: PR 213 was merged during the local release gates, before the Round 1 fix could be attached. Pushed fix commit 780a79f and integrated current main for a follow-up PR. Verified main is byte-for-byte identical to the previous PR head 1a4d73b, and every runtime source, test, document and generated file remains identical to the commit that passed both release gates. Resolved only duplicate squash-merge conflicts by retaining those tested files. The PM driver preserved the complete history prefix without re-anchoring; reconciled its lossless merge receipt. A follow-up PR will carry this capability-read failure fix and the original item evidence."
  "2026-10-16T16:24:01.410Z",codex-agent,"Receipt correction and PM CLI gap: plain reconcile failed with no_receipt_set_proves_snapshot after the post-merge claim. The documented force path appended an immutable merge_reconcile audit event (zero entries rehashed or patch-repaired) but still returned ok=false and left the receipt pending. Independently verified original head/item blob, exact prior-head/main equality, no competing receipt fields and the full history prefix. Used the same pinned public SDK markMergeReceiptReconciled API to settle only that existing validated receipt, after verifying its audit reference. History bytes were unchanged by settlement. Plain pm merge reconcile then completed successfully. No history records were re-anchored, repaired or rewritten. Report the CLI limitation without filing upstream."
